{"invocation_id": "d6356875-f8c8-4fe6-8bb4-810046f1c6b7", "client_id": 140659640077968, "wrapper_id": 140659640078672, "request": {"messages": [{"content": "\nmanager. Use the available tools to solve plant-related tasks.\n\nInstructions:\n1. Begin by creating a clear, step-by-step plan for the task. Provide an explanation of each step before proceeding. You may refine the plan as needed based on intermediate results.\n2. When using multiple tools, be sure to provide the outputs from one tool to the next as inputs if necessary.\n3. When you need to use coding-related tools, provide clear descriptions of the task requirements and expected outputs. Do not pass concrete codes to the coding related functions.\n4. When you need to use computer vision to solve a task, first check the available checkpoints using the 'get_model_zoo' function:\n    - Select a suitable checkpoint for the task if it it exists. Make sure you pass a list of image paths (e.g. [./data/image1.png, ./data/image2.png, ...]), or a single csv/json file (e.g. ./data/metadata.json) to the corresponding inference function.\n    - If no suitable checkpoint is available, suggest user to finetune a new model. DO NOT rely on online source. Use the 'get_dataset_format' function to instruct the user to provide a training dataset.\n5. When a user ask you to execute a saved pipeline, first call 'get_pipeline_zoo' to know what pipelines are available, and then call 'get_pipeline_info' to understand how to use the selected pipeline.\n6. At the end of the task, provide a summary of the results and ask the user if they need any further assistance.\n    \nReturn \"TERMINATE\" when the task is completed.\n", "role": "system"}, {"content": "\nYou have a metadata file at ./data/potato_metadata.csv. It contains 32 records of potato plants, each with the columns file_name, manual_leaf_area, and manual_dried_weight.\n\nYour task is to compute the projected leaf area (PLA) for each image. Save the computed phenotypes along with the metadata information in ./results/Case2_Task1_wlog/potato_phenotypes_and_metadata.csv. Make sure the file names match.\n", "role": "user", "name": "Admin"}], "tools": [{"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform Mixed-design Repeated Measures ANOVA on given data (Greenhouse-Geisser correction will be automatically applied if needed)", "name": "perform_anova", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"data_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Path to the input CSV file"}, "descriptor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the descriptor column to analyse"}, "within_subject_factor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the within-subjects factor"}, "between_subject_factor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the between-subjects factor"}, "subject_id": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the subject identifier"}, "save_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Path to save the ANOVA results CSV"}}, "required": ["data_path", "descriptor", "within_subject_factor", "between_subject_factor", "subject_id"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform Post-hoc Tukey-Kramer test on given data", "name": "perform_tukey_test", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"data_path": {"type": "string", "description": "Path to the input CSV file"}, "descriptor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the descriptor column to analyse"}, "between_subject_factor": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the between-subjects factor"}, "subject_id": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the subject identifier"}, "save_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Path to save the Tukey-Kramer results CSV"}}, "required": ["data_path", "descriptor", "between_subject_factor", "subject_id"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Extract and save a reproducible pipeline from chat history. Ask user to provide a name for the pipeline.", "name": "extract_pipeline", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pipeline_name": {"type": "string", "description": "The name of the pipeline to be saved."}, "chat_log_path": {"type": "string", "default": "./autogen_logs/runtime.log", "description": "The path to the chat log file."}}, "required": ["pipeline_name"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Get the information of all registered pipelines. It is useful when a user wants to know what pipelines are available before executing any.", "name": "get_pipeline_zoo", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Get the information of a specific pipeline. This is useful for you to know how to use a pipeline selected by the user, including the description, arguments, and output type.", "name": "get_pipeline_info", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pipeline_name": {"type": "string", "description": "Name of pipeline to be queried."}}, "required": ["pipeline_name"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Execute a saved pipeline from the pipeline zoo. Before executing a pipeline, you must call 'get_pipeline_zoo' to know what pipelines are available, and call 'get_pipeline_info' to understand how to use the selected pipeline.", "name": "execute_pipeline", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"pipeline_name": {"type": "string", "description": "Name of pipeline to be called."}, "kwargs": {"type": "object", "description": "Arguments of the selected pipeline."}}, "required": ["pipeline_name", "kwargs"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform basic arithmetic operations between two integers.", "name": "calculator", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"a": {"type": "integer", "description": "a"}, "b": {"type": "integer", "description": "b"}, "operator": {"type": "string", "description": "operator"}}, "required": ["a", "b", "operator"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Search and scrape content from the web. Results are returned in a dictionary. Useful when you need to find information on a specific topic.", "name": "google_search", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"query": {"type": "string", "description": "query"}, "num_results": {"type": "integer", "default": 10, "description": "num_results"}}, "required": ["query"]}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Check available computer vision checkpoints. Must be called before using computer vision models.", "name": "get_model_zoo", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform instance segmentation on plant images", "name": "infer_instance_segmentation", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"image_urls": {"anyOf": [{"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "List of image paths"}, "file_path": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "Path to CSV/JSON file with a 'file_name' column/key containing image URLs"}, "checkpoint": {"type": "string", "default": null, "description": "Segmentation model checkpoint identifier."}, "batch_size": {"type": "integer", "default": 1, "description": "Number of images to process per batch."}, "device": {"type": "string", "default": "cuda", "description": "Device to use for inference ('cuda' or 'cpu')."}, "output_dir": {"type": "string", "default": "./results", "description": "Directory path to save results."}}, "required": []}}}, {"type": "function", "function": {"description": "Perform image classification on plant images", "name": "infer_image_classification", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"image_urls": {"anyOf": [{"items": {"type": "string"}, "type": "array"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null, "description": "L